In @.agents/skills/architect/SKILL.md:
- Around line 11-13: Update the “Stateful vs. Stateless Segregation” guidance to
distinguish stateless JWKS/token verification, which remains in the native
in-process SDK, from stateful identity data and mutations such as tenant
provisioning, persistence, and tenant resolution. Explicitly require tenant
state to be centralized behind a language-agnostic service or port so
implementations cannot maintain divergent tenant mappings.

In @.agents/skills/cloud-architect/SKILL.md:
- Line 12: Update the “Compute Isolation & Queuing” guidance to avoid implying
that choosing SQS or RabbitMQ alone prevents data loss. State that burst
absorption and delivery guarantees additionally depend on durable configuration,
producer confirmations, retention, dead-letter replay, retry/backoff, and
idempotent consumers.

